  "title": "EgoMemReason and FlashBack",
  "summary": "EgoMemReason establishes a benchmark for week-long egocentric video understanding, while FlashBack introduces a training-free framework for selective, multi-level memory in streaming vision-language models. Both aim to enhance long-term memory efficiency and agent performance in complex tasks.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "EgoMemReason evaluates 17 methods across MLLMs and agentic frameworks, revealing that long-horizon memory remains challenging.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "FlashBack introduces a framework for selective, multi-level memory in streaming vision-language models, addressing the tension between real-time perception and long-term memory.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "FlashBack dynamically determines whether inference remains on the Native trajectory or invokes an isolated Recall trajectory.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
